1
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:03,380
Previously on "Final Space"...

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:05,030
Nightfall reveals
that she's Quinn?

3
00:00:05,070 --> 00:00:06,310
From the future?!

4
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:07,660
Whoa! Hot diggity!

5
00:00:07,690 --> 00:00:09,690
Also, she has a thing for Gary,

6
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:11,830
but there's no time
for cosmic three-ways...

7
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:15,730
because our crew has a breach
to close in space...

8
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:17,050
and fast.

9
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:19,360
♪♪

10
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:24,160
H.U.E.: Gary, you have
two minutes of oxygen left.

11
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:27,190
[ Breathing heavily ]

12
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:29,020
Can we...

13
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:31,510
change that
to something more cheerful?

14
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:33,270
Sure, Gary.

15
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,580
Cookies.

16
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:37,170
Act like you're baking
a big batch of cookies.

17
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,790
Gary, the cookies will be done
in two minutes.

18
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,900
Oh...fantastic.

19
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:45,870
I love cookies.

20
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,460
What kind of cookies
we talkin' about?

21
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:50,530
Butter wheat crunch.

22
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:53,460
That's...not a cookie.

23
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,120
And you know that, H.U.E.

24
00:00:56,150 --> 00:00:57,950
You know that!

25
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:07,130
♪♪

26
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:16,380
♪♪

27
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:25,840
♪♪

28
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,290
♪♪

29
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,840
Gary: Crew!

30
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:33,160
Or legion of murdering
an irritatingly power-thirsty

31
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:36,510
pint-sized imp
into a plethora of buttholes!

32
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:38,580
Are you ready
to save the Earth?!

33
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,920
-Hooray! Oh, yeah!
-Hooray! Hooray!

34
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:43,340
The question is, Captain,
are youready?

35
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:45,270
I'm so ready!

36
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:46,580
I'm so not ready!

37
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:48,660
How am I gonna save
an entire planet?

38
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:50,110
I'm all for trying,

39
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:53,830
but there's a high chance
we're all going to die!

40
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:56,490
Yes. It's more or less
a done deal.

41
00:01:56,530 --> 00:01:58,530
That's not comforting
at all!

42
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,940
I can do this, right?
Right?!

43
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:02,980
Oh, this is impossible!

44
00:02:03,010 --> 00:02:05,600
Nothing is impossible

45
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,020
if we apply our minds to it.

46
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:11,440
H.U.E., do we know of a way
we can close this breach?

47
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:13,340
No.Well, that's not good.

48
00:02:13,370 --> 00:02:14,610
Okay, uh, well...

49
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:16,060
anything at all
we could do?

50
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:18,620
Yes. You can kiss
your cheeks goodbye.

51
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:20,000
You givin' me
a little clap back?

52
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:22,170
You givin' me
the old clap back, H.U.E.?!

53
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:23,550
I thought I'd give it a try

54
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:25,800
before we implode
into nothingness.

55
00:02:25,830 --> 00:02:30,560
"Implode into nothingness,"
he said!

56
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:33,390
Oh, my gosh.
Freaking Mondays.

57
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,500
Gary,
am I gonna die?

58
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,010
Are you trying
to cheer me up, KVN?

59
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:40,290
Okay, because you dying would
be a wonderful development.

60
00:02:40,330 --> 00:02:42,470
♪ We're all gonna die

61
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:43,680
♪ We're all gonna di--

62
00:02:43,710 --> 00:02:45,060
Shut the hell up, KVN.

63
00:02:45,090 --> 00:02:47,160
Or I will find ways.

64
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,750
Actually, there is a way.

65
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:53,690
H.U.E., set coordinates
for sector 12, region 6.79.

66
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:57,310
Nightfall, that would fly us
directly into the sun

67
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:58,860
at the heart
of the Orion Nebula.

68
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:02,660
I know.We are not flying
into a sun!

69
00:03:02,690 --> 00:03:03,730
Do you want to live?

70
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,250
Yes.
I would love to live.

71
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:09,050
That's exactly freaking why
we're not flying into a sun!

72
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,600
You're right.
We're going to lightfold in.

73
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:14,570
That's freaking worse!

74
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,430
You said it
like it was better,

75
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:18,430
but that is
the opposite of better!

76
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:19,780
I would never suggest this

77
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:22,060
unless I knew something
you're not sharing.

78
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:23,200
What do you know?

79
00:03:23,230 --> 00:03:27,060
Quinn, aren't you curious
how you became me?

80
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,550
If that answers even
involves flying into a sun,

81
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:30,760
I'm not curious.

82
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:31,900
I don't think
anybody's curious.

83
00:03:31,930 --> 00:03:33,350
Aah!I'm curious!
Keep going!

84
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,930
[ Cackles ]
-Must you, KVN?!

85
00:03:34,970 --> 00:03:37,040
Must you?!
Hee-hee hoo.

86
00:03:37,070 --> 00:03:38,040
Tell me.

87
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:40,700
There's only one being
who can help us.

88
00:03:40,730 --> 00:03:42,110
A Titan
who inhabits a realm

89
00:03:42,150 --> 00:03:45,050
between our dimension and
the next called Inner Space.

90
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,640
He came to me.

91
00:03:46,670 --> 00:03:49,120
At my lowest point.

92
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:56,610
♪♪

93
00:03:56,650 --> 00:03:58,410
It's over.

94
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:00,580
Everything is over.

95
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:02,240
♪♪

96
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:03,760
I'm coming, Gary.

97
00:04:03,790 --> 00:04:07,550
Bolo:
This is not your fate.

98
00:04:07,590 --> 00:04:11,760
I offer not madness,
but salvation.

99
00:04:13,110 --> 00:04:15,660
We can change
what has become.

100
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:19,390
How?A machine to traverse time.

101
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:21,080
You can construct it.

102
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,120
With my help.

103
00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:25,570
Who are you?
Bolo.

104
00:04:25,610 --> 00:04:28,470
A fellow victim of infinity.

105
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,850
And now we fight back.

106
00:04:31,890 --> 00:04:34,750
Little Cato: Who's Bolo?He's a Titan.

107
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:37,000
The Titans are
terrible, vengeful creatures

108
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:39,860
who poison the universe
with chaos.

109
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:42,280
Each in charge
of a different realm.

110
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:44,450
One broke ranks.

111
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:46,320
Bolo.

112
00:04:46,350 --> 00:04:48,870
He saw there was a better way
and sealed off our dimension

113
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:50,940
from the horrors of Final Space.

114
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:53,870
They took revenge
and imprisoned him.

115
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:56,190
He's the only one
who can help.

116
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:57,840
[ Laughs ]
That's sick.

117
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,050
Older hot Quinn
makes an excellent point.

118
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:03,060
If Bolo's the only one
that can help us,

119
00:05:03,090 --> 00:05:04,370
we've got no choice.

120
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:06,510
Chookity pok!Well said, Mooncake.

121
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:08,510
Let's fly through a sun!

122
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:09,790
Oh, my Lord,

123
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:11,930
I cannot believe
we are doing this.

124
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,070
♪♪

125
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,800
Dimension phasing
is notoriously difficult.

126
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:19,690
To see Bolo, we're going
to have to lightfold

127
00:05:19,730 --> 00:05:21,520
exactly through
the sun's aperture.

128
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:25,800
If we are off by even one
degree, we burn up and die.

129
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:28,460
Buckle up.
This will be a bumpy ride.

130
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:31,080
All right, H.U.E.
Take us in!

131
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:34,160
♪♪

132
00:05:34,190 --> 00:05:37,370
Entering into the corona
of the sun.

133
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:42,480
♪♪

134
00:05:42,510 --> 00:05:45,750
The heat of the sun has melted
through the navigation system.

135
00:05:45,790 --> 00:05:48,930
You will need to manually
navigate it into the aperture.

136
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:50,830
All right, I'll do it.

137
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:52,280
But you're not a good pilot.

138
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:55,280
Thank you very much for
believing in me, Quinn.

139
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,730
Please do not screw this up.

140
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:58,250
Okay, that's not helping!

141
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,350
Concentrate, Gary.

142
00:05:59,390 --> 00:06:00,490
You gotta do this.

143
00:06:00,530 --> 00:06:01,940
Let's thread this needle.

144
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:05,190
♪♪

145
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:06,910
[ Grunting ]

146
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:09,120
Come on, come on,
come on, come on!

147
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:14,680
♪♪

148
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:16,270
[ Screaming ]

149
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,370
Gary! Center it!

150
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:18,440
I got this!

151
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,060
You got this,
Thunder Bandit!

152
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:21,860
Quinn: No, you don't!
Center it!

153
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:23,380
Oh, you're scaring me!
I'm scared!

154
00:06:23,410 --> 00:06:24,410
Center it!

155
00:06:24,450 --> 00:06:25,590
I'm very frightened!

156
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:27,620
Gary!
Aah!

157
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,700
Oh, my crap!

158
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:33,150
Oh, my crap.

159
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,700
♪♪

160
00:06:34,730 --> 00:06:38,220
Welcome to Inner Space.

161
00:06:38,250 --> 00:06:41,840
♪♪

162
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,810
♪♪

163
00:06:45,850 --> 00:06:47,920
Just our luck.
He's asleep.

164
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,650
Gary, he's been asleep
for 10,000 years.

165
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:53,060
Well, then
why are we here?

166
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,960
Wait for it.

167
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,450
Wait for wha--

168
00:06:57,480 --> 00:07:01,170
[ All shouting ]

169
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:08,080
[ Voices distorting ]

170
00:07:08,110 --> 00:07:11,180
[ Rumbling ]

171
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:13,570
Get me the hell out of here!

172
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:18,500
♪♪

173
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:22,680
Did we just get sucked
into dude's mind?

174
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:23,850
Don't worry,
that's normal.

175
00:07:23,890 --> 00:07:25,750
I am not okay with this --

176
00:07:25,790 --> 00:07:30,380
winter wonderland
of cosmic cotton candy!

177
00:07:30,410 --> 00:07:32,380
Aah! Aah!

178
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:36,490
I'm just gonna put this down
right on this little lily pad.

179
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,350
Oh, there we go.

180
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:40,110
[ Sighs ]

181
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:46,500
♪♪

182
00:07:46,530 --> 00:07:48,390
Oh, hey,
there's a guy.

183
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:49,950
Hey. Hey!

184
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:52,230
So, not sure we're
in the right place,

185
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:53,850
but we got this thing --

186
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,330
You're late!

187
00:07:55,370 --> 00:07:57,510
-Late?
-Yes, late!

188
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,820
He's been waiting
on you for years!

189
00:07:59,850 --> 00:08:01,890
You're like
a giant flaming M&M.

190
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:05,130
Excuse me?!
Are you giving me sass?!

191
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:06,240
Hyah!
[ Grunts ]

192
00:08:06,270 --> 00:08:07,720
Oh! Freaking!
Did you just

193
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,350
whack me in the face
with your stick?!

194
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:11,070
Aah!

195
00:08:11,110 --> 00:08:13,760
You and I are not
gonna get along.

196
00:08:14,730 --> 00:08:18,010
[ All shouting ]

197
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,980
Explain...

198
00:08:22,010 --> 00:08:23,570
to me...

199
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,810
what just happened.

200
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:27,020
We hopped over
to brain chamber two.

201
00:08:27,050 --> 00:08:28,160
Hopped?

202
00:08:28,190 --> 00:08:29,500
No, no, no, no!

203
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:31,890
We were hurled --

204
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:37,930
Oh, there's moisture.

205
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:38,930
[ Gasps ]

206
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:40,890
I think my eyes are bleeding!

207
00:08:40,930 --> 00:08:42,210
[ Laughing hysterically ]

208
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,210
My eyes!

209
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,110
Blood! Blood!

210
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:48,700
[ Chuckles ] This is only
Brain Chamber Six.

211
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:54,050
[ All shouting ]

212
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:01,670
Here we are
Chamber number 795.

213
00:09:01,710 --> 00:09:03,680
Bolo's Mind Palace.

214
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:06,960
Beyond this point,
only one of you may enter,

215
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:10,100
and it's already
been pre-selected.

216
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:13,310
Yooooooooou!

217
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,140
You've been chosen.

218
00:09:15,170 --> 00:09:17,860
But then again,
you were already selected

219
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:20,900
before you were even born!

220
00:09:20,930 --> 00:09:23,140
-We'll be here, Gary.
-You got this!

221
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:24,420
[ Mooncake cooing ]

222
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:25,970
[ Grunts ] Hee-hee-hee!

223
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:27,980
KVN will look after Mooncake,
'cause he's so helpful.

224
00:09:28,010 --> 00:09:30,980
♪ Oh, baby,
KVN's got the magic ♪

225
00:09:31,010 --> 00:09:32,880
♪ And the magic's got KVN

226
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:33,980
I don't like this.

227
00:09:34,020 --> 00:09:35,570
All this right here,
I don't like.

228
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,050
You're not hanging
out with Mooncake.

229
00:09:37,090 --> 00:09:39,230
You're a bad influence. Okay?
'Cause I don't like you.

230
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:43,270
♪ Oh, baby, KVN's got the magic,
and the magic's got KVN ♪

231
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:46,170
♪ KVN's got the magic,
and magic's got KVN ♪

232
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,650
You're the worst.

233
00:09:47,690 --> 00:09:49,510
Good luck, Gary.

234
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:53,690
[ Whirring ]

235
00:09:56,660 --> 00:09:59,320
♪♪

236
00:09:59,350 --> 00:10:01,600
Bolo: Come forth, Gary.

237
00:10:01,630 --> 00:10:04,630
♪♪

238
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:06,950
Oh, my gosh. Okay.

239
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,260
Ohh...

240
00:10:08,290 --> 00:10:10,640
Oh -- ah!

241
00:10:10,670 --> 00:10:11,640
Aah!

242
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,190
Okay. This is new.

243
00:10:13,230 --> 00:10:15,260
Bolo: In order
to face what's ahead,

244
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:19,200
you need to face
what's inside of you.

245
00:10:19,230 --> 00:10:20,300
[ Gasps ]

246
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:21,550
Oh, look!

247
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:23,860
There's
a Construction Hat Gary.

248
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:24,930
Hey!

249
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:27,210
[ Gasps ]
There's an Eagle-Faced Gary.

250
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:28,550
[ Screeching ] Hi!

251
00:10:28,590 --> 00:10:30,350
[ Gasps ]
Cookie-Headed Gary.

252
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,760
Hi. What's up?

253
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:33,520
Oh, my gosh!

254
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,110
Little Micro Gary.

255
00:10:35,150 --> 00:10:36,940
-[ High-pitched ] Hey!
-Who's that?

256
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:39,560
Bolo: That's
the Amazing Mustache Gary.

257
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:43,710
Gary, you're never gonna
be able to grow one of these.

258
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:49,470
A thick, rich,
luscious mustache.

259
00:10:49,510 --> 00:10:51,780
[ Moans ]

260
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:54,550
[ Moans ] Hell yeah,
that feels good!

261
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:55,860
It's true.

262
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:57,410
I've never been able
to grow a mustache.

263
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:03,040
I wish I was a crumb,
so I could get caught in this.

264
00:11:03,070 --> 00:11:04,380
What are you doing,
Mustache Gary?

265
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:08,840
Combing my Mustache with
my Little Mustache Comb!

266
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:12,740
But you'll never know
the satisfaction of that.

267
00:11:12,770 --> 00:11:14,910
[ Laughs ]

268
00:11:14,950 --> 00:11:18,360
Oh, it feels
so gooooood!

269
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:20,090
Ugh, it's so true.

270
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,750
I won't.

271
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:23,540
[ Groans ] Oh, no.

272
00:11:23,570 --> 00:11:24,850
What is this?

273
00:11:24,890 --> 00:11:26,090
Aah! What's happening?!

274
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:28,820
Bolo: Your anxiety
is consuming you.

275
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:31,620
-[ Groans ]
-You know you can't succeed.

276
00:11:31,650 --> 00:11:33,720
Because I can't
grow a 'stache?

277
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:37,690
That's exactly why.
[ Laughs ]

278
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:42,180
Bolo: You're not hero.

279
00:11:42,210 --> 00:11:45,290
Your father was.

280
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:47,250
[ Gasping ]

281
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:49,050
You're right.

282
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:51,290
He would've
figured this out.

283
00:11:51,330 --> 00:11:54,050
I'm scared there's
no winning this,

284
00:11:54,090 --> 00:11:55,780
that there's no way
to close this breach

285
00:11:55,810 --> 00:11:58,750
without losing my friends.

286
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:00,470
Okay.

287
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:02,030
Let's not
do that again!

288
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:05,410
All progress begins
with the truth.

289
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,580
We're running
out of time.

290
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:10,970
I need to know right now
how to close this breach.

291
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:14,590
I don't have the answer for you,
but he will.

292
00:12:14,630 --> 00:12:17,590
Who the hell is "He Will?"
I don't know a "He Will."

293
00:12:17,630 --> 00:12:20,560
You'll only have
a short time.

294
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:24,810
[ Whirring ]

295
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:31,160
Hello?

296
00:12:31,190 --> 00:12:37,790
♪♪

297
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:39,170
Dad.

298
00:12:41,450 --> 00:12:42,830
What's going on
with Gary?

299
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:45,240
-He's fine.
-Show them, Gatekeeper.

300
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:46,590
Reveal your secrets!

301
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:49,490
And if you hit me,
I will end you.

302
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:52,800
Oh, my gosh!
You are all so sassy!

303
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:56,120
Just watch
and leave me alone already.

304
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:59,190
Bolo:
Mooncake, follow my voice.

305
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:01,910
-Chockity.
-KVN, stop touching stuff.

306
00:13:01,950 --> 00:13:04,190
♪ And the magic's got KVN

307
00:13:04,230 --> 00:13:05,190
Everybody!

308
00:13:05,230 --> 00:13:07,470
Dad, it's me, Gary.

309
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:09,470
Dad?
Who the hell are you?

310
00:13:09,510 --> 00:13:11,340
And why did time freeze?

311
00:13:11,370 --> 00:13:12,790
Did you freeze time?

312
00:13:12,820 --> 00:13:14,440
You time-freezing demon!

313
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,270
Whoa! Okay, look.
I don't think you would

314
00:13:16,310 --> 00:13:18,280
believe me if I told you
how I got here.

315
00:13:18,310 --> 00:13:20,830
But I'm telling you
I am your son.

316
00:13:20,860 --> 00:13:24,660
My son is much younger,
a boy half your age.

317
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:28,350
If you're really my son,
what was the promise?

318
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:29,980
What?
Before I left.

319
00:13:30,010 --> 00:13:31,980
To have my adventures.

320
00:13:32,010 --> 00:13:35,530
Bunches and bunches
of them.

321
00:13:35,570 --> 00:13:37,190
Is it really you?

322
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:39,370
As real as it gets, Dad.

323
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:45,720
Oh, hell yeah.

324
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:48,170
♪♪

325
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,890
What the hell
are you doing here?

326
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:52,210
It's a real novel, but I'm
trying to save the Earth --

327
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:54,590
actually universe sounds
way cooler,

328
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:57,000
so I'm actually gonna say
"universe" from now on.

329
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,350
You're what?

330
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:00,730
I'm trying to find out how
to close a breach in space

331
00:14:00,770 --> 00:14:02,560
that will most certainly
destroy Earth --

332
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,390
actually universe --
in my time.

333
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:05,740
God, that sounds so cool.

334
00:14:05,770 --> 00:14:08,600
I really feel cool
saying that out loud.

335
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:09,770
Well, that's what
I'm doing now!

336
00:14:09,810 --> 00:14:11,740
What?You're doing what I'm doing.

337
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:13,500
I'm doing what you're doing!No way!

338
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:15,230
Look!

339
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:17,400
You're closing
the breach in space?

340
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,410
Me and my co-pilot, yeah.

341
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:26,410
♪♪

342
00:14:26,450 --> 00:14:33,350
♪♪

343
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:34,420
What is he doing here?!

344
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:35,800
Jack's my co-pilot.

345
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,700
We've been doing missions
together for years.

346
00:14:37,730 --> 00:14:40,910
Jack?! This guy
is the Lord Commander!

347
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:43,080
-Who?
-The guy who ripped my arm off

348
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:45,710
with his mind
and killed my best friend.

349
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:47,120
Jack is my co-pilot.

350
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:50,890
He's been my friend
for 29 years.

351
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,750
But I'll take
your word for it.

352
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:55,610
Well, what do you say we beat
the crap out of him, son?

353
00:14:55,650 --> 00:14:58,200
You are my dad.

354
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,790
Hey!

355
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,240
You sick sack of --

356
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:02,380
Gah!

357
00:15:02,410 --> 00:15:03,620
Ha! Heyyy!

358
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:04,930
Heyyyyyy!

359
00:15:04,970 --> 00:15:06,590
Multiple punches
in the face!

360
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:10,110
Every boy dreams of building
cherished memories...

361
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:11,840
-Harder!
-...with his dad.

362
00:15:11,870 --> 00:15:14,460
-Like this.
-Kick him in the nuts!

363
00:15:14,490 --> 00:15:15,630
Oh, and this!

364
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:16,740
Oh, and these!

365
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:18,640
-[ Laughs ]
-Hyah!

366
00:15:18,670 --> 00:15:21,780
-That's my boy.
-[ Laughs ]

367
00:15:21,810 --> 00:15:23,500
When was the last time
you saw me?

368
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:26,440
Right before
this mission.

369
00:15:26,470 --> 00:15:27,610
You never came back.

370
00:15:27,650 --> 00:15:28,820
Hm.

371
00:15:28,850 --> 00:15:30,960
So, I'm about to die,
huh?

372
00:15:30,990 --> 00:15:32,480
Not if I can help it.

373
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:34,760
So how are we gonna
close this breach?

374
00:15:34,790 --> 00:15:36,310
I need to know for me.

375
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,970
An anti-matter bomb
detonated

376
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,970
at the event horizon
of the breach.

377
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,250
The thing is,
right before you came aboard,

378
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:45,530
an energy blast in Final Space
was about to hit our ship.

379
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:48,600
Time froze, and now there's
no way to deliver the bomb.

380
00:15:48,630 --> 00:15:50,320
Unless...
Hit me.

381
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,500
[ Thwack! ]
Nice.

382
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:54,670
Thanks. What if you take out
the bomb manually?

383
00:15:54,710 --> 00:15:56,120
That could work.
Really?

384
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:59,510
Wow, I mean,
we could do it together.

385
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:01,820
Bolo: Mooncake.

386
00:16:01,850 --> 00:16:03,270
It's time you knew.

387
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:05,100
Whoa, look at all
this cool brain stuff.

388
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:09,340
Hmm. That's mine, and that's
mine, and that's mine.

389
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,900
Hey, let's do Jell-O shots
with the grain goo!

390
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:17,010
You're the key
to Final Space...

391
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:19,870
because that's what
you're made of.

392
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,670
Final Space.

393
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:28,330
♪♪

394
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:31,090
Chockity.

395
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:36,020
We'll need to take out the
primary and secondary trigger.

396
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:38,030
Right. I have no idea
what that is,

397
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:41,550
so I'm gonna look at you
and nod in agreement.

398
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:44,550
So, you met anybody?

399
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:46,030
No, well, kind of.

400
00:16:46,070 --> 00:16:48,210
I'm seeing two people
at the same time -- but mainly,

401
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:51,250
I'm not like cheating because
they're the same person.

402
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:53,040
Got it.
Time-travel thing?

403
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:55,040
Yes!
Been there.

404
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:57,250
Ha! [ Laughs ]

405
00:16:57,290 --> 00:16:58,600
Nice pair.

406
00:16:58,630 --> 00:17:00,050
What's their name?
Quinn.

407
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,570
What's she like?

408
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,190
The younger hot one?
Or the older equally hot one?

409
00:17:04,230 --> 00:17:05,710
The one in your
timeline.

410
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:09,750
Well, she's headstrong,
focused, and a real leader.

411
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:10,960
Do you love her?
Ohh!

412
00:17:10,990 --> 00:17:13,200
[ Laughs nervously ]
To the max-core.

413
00:17:13,230 --> 00:17:17,100
But I don't think she thinks
very much of me.

414
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:18,790
Really? You're a catch.

415
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:20,240
You think I'm a catch?
You -- you think so?

416
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,930
I'm looking at you,
I'm seeing a catch.

417
00:17:23,970 --> 00:17:25,520
All right,
it's ready to go.

418
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:28,350
You sure there isn't anything
else that needs to be done?

419
00:17:28,390 --> 00:17:30,730
Bomb-wise?
Anything else at all?

420
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:32,120
That's it. Let's go.

421
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:33,700
We could get lunch.

422
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:36,120
You want to get lunch?

423
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,090
Son.

424
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:42,640
Grab the plasma torch.

425
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:46,090
♪♪

426
00:17:46,130 --> 00:17:48,300
What are you doing?
Dad!

427
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:50,100
Dad, don't do this
without me!

428
00:17:50,130 --> 00:17:52,100
[ Grunts ]Son, you have your own time

429
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:53,550
to worry about.

430
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:55,410
[ Grunting ]

431
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:57,110
Dad! This --

432
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:58,280
This was my idea.

433
00:17:58,310 --> 00:18:00,280
Yeah, but it's
my responsibility.

434
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:02,800
There's another
anti-matter bomb in New York.

435
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:04,110
The one on Earth.

436
00:18:04,150 --> 00:18:07,080
Use it to close
this breach in your time.

437
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:10,290
You know, I had only
one regret when I left.

438
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:12,090
Thought I was never
gonna get the chance

439
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:14,330
to see the man
you would've grown up to be.

440
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:19,300
Well, now I know he's better
than I would've ever hoped.

441
00:18:19,330 --> 00:18:20,990
Please don't.
Stop. Please.

442
00:18:21,030 --> 00:18:23,820
Stop. Stop. Stop! Stop!

443
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:25,650
No! Please no!

444
00:18:25,690 --> 00:18:27,520
Stop!

445
00:18:27,550 --> 00:18:29,410
[ Beeps ]

446
00:18:29,450 --> 00:18:31,170
♪♪

447
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:32,660
I'm not gonna let you die.

448
00:18:32,690 --> 00:18:34,110
Not again.

449
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:35,830
I'm gonna come get you!

450
00:18:35,870 --> 00:18:37,870
Make me a promise,
son.

451
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:39,600
Save the Earth.

452
00:18:39,630 --> 00:18:41,150
Nah, you're right.

453
00:18:41,180 --> 00:18:43,150
"Universe"
sounds much cooler.

454
00:18:43,190 --> 00:18:45,530
What if I can't do it?

455
00:18:45,570 --> 00:18:47,160
Try your best.

456
00:18:47,190 --> 00:18:49,950
What if my best
isn't good enough?

457
00:18:49,990 --> 00:18:52,020
It's good enough
for me.

458
00:18:52,060 --> 00:19:03,480
♪♪

459
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:14,730
♪♪

460
00:19:14,770 --> 00:19:17,700
Noooooooooo!

461
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:19,670
No.

462
00:19:19,710 --> 00:19:21,850
♪♪

463
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,020
Aaah!

464
00:19:23,050 --> 00:19:25,330
Oh, God!

465
00:19:25,370 --> 00:19:28,680
Aaaah!

466
00:19:28,710 --> 00:19:30,750
[ Snarls ]

467
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:38,690
♪♪

468
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:53,530
♪♪

469
00:19:53,570 --> 00:19:56,600
[ Sobbing ]

470
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,570
Why?

471
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:04,130
Didn't know we were members
of the same club.

472
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:07,100
Gary, you still
want to do this?

473
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:11,340
I'll try my best.

474
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:13,070
That's good enough
for me.

475
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,110
Wait -- were you watching
me and my dad?

476
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:16,380
No.

477
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,520
No.

478
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:22,910
♪♪

479
00:20:22,940 --> 00:20:24,740
Where are you going?

480
00:20:24,770 --> 00:20:27,430
They don't need
me anymore.

481
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:39,580
♪♪

482
00:20:39,610 --> 00:20:41,060
Should we get up?

483
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:43,310
No. We have
a little time.

484
00:20:43,340 --> 00:20:45,070
Actually, you don't!

485
00:20:45,100 --> 00:20:47,450
Get off
your sass buckets!!

486
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,420
♪♪

487
00:20:50,450 --> 00:20:53,630
H.U.E.: Gary, is Nightfall
not coming with us?

488
00:20:53,660 --> 00:20:55,010
No.

489
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:56,490
You think you know a person,

490
00:20:56,530 --> 00:20:58,910
and then something
like this happens.

491
00:20:58,940 --> 00:21:00,430
What course
should I set?

492
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:01,320
Earth.

493
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:03,120
Or actually,
no, the Universe.

494
00:21:03,150 --> 00:21:04,470
We're gonna save the --
Well actually,

495
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:05,950
well, that's doesn't even
make any dang sense.

496
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:07,780
Okay, just Earth.
Earth...

497
00:21:07,810 --> 00:21:08,780
Earth.

498
00:21:08,810 --> 00:21:10,780
We've got a bomb to find.

499
00:21:10,820 --> 00:21:17,440
♪♪
